    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2553, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7689\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to the membership\nof the early intervention coordinating council\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo add representatives of managed care plans or managed care plan\ntrade associations who work in the early intervention field as members\nof the early intervention coordinating council.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 1 of section 2553 of the public health\nlaw in order to add three representatives from managed care or managed\ncare trade associations who work in the early intervention field as\nmembers of the early intervention coordinating council.\n\nSection 2: Provides the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Assembly Oversight, Analysis and Investigation Committee and the\nHealth Committee hosted a roundtable discussion to gather insight on\nthe experiences and challenges of the Early Intervention Program's\nfiscal agent system. Representatives of the fiscal agent, EI providers\nand provider associations, county and New York City health officials,\nand other stakeholders came to the table to share their perspectives\nand recommendations about the program and the fiscal agent system. One\nof the recommendations that was made was to provide a mechanism to\nopen the public dialogue between managed care plans, early\nintervention providers, and the Department of Health. One way to do\nthis would be to have representatives from managed care plans be\nmembers of the Early Intervention Coordinating Council. This would\nprovide managed care plans and trade associations, who are an\nimportant stakeholder, the opportunity to hear the experiences and\nconcerns of providers, as well as give them a voice at the table to\nrespond, in order to help make the reimbursement system operate more\neffectively.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nOn the one hundred eightieth day after enactment.\n",
